From 6505aaec88684aada3d87c8139c0266cbdbdd01d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 18:47:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] estserver: an optional wire log of the attest-* exchanges, as
 they crossed the wire

A new optional setting, wire_log (est.ServerConfig.WireLog), makes the server write one JSON object per line for
every exchange on an attest-* resource, with or without the additional path segment: the request's method, path,
query, Content-Type and body, and the response's status, Content-Type and body. It lets the bench check each message
of a hardware run against the draft's CDDL, and an interop partner see exactly what went over the wire.

The record does not change the exchange: the middleware reads the request body ahead of the handler and gives the
handler the same bytes, and the same error when the body ends in one (the 64 KiB limit's), and takes the response
with chi's Tee. Other resources pass unrecorded. Nothing recorded is secret from the EST server, which TACRA treats
as a conduit; headers other than Content-Type, Authorization among them, are not recorded.

Checked: go vet; go test ./internal/tacra ./cmd/estserver ./internal/refvectors: ok. TestWireLogRecordsTheExchange
serves five requests through the server's own router and this backend, with the log and without it: the same status,
Content-Type and body each time; the four attest-* exchanges recorded as sent and answered (the enrollment request a
real one, the reference implementation's from GCP SEV-SNP), including one under a CA label and one over the size limit
(the 65536 octets the server read, and its 400); /cacerts not recorded.
